00:05:00.078 --> 00:05:02.308
- So I was watching my
brother play this video game

00:05:02.308 --> 00:05:03.378
and he used a cheat code

00:05:03.378 --> 00:05:05.668
that let his character do
a walk through walls hack.

00:05:05.668 --> 00:05:07.228
He pushed himself against a barrier

00:05:07.228 --> 00:05:08.624
in the game, hit some buttons and boom,

00:05:08.624 --> 00:05:10.758
his character appeared on the other side.

00:05:10.758 --> 00:05:13.148
Imagine if he could walk
through walls in real life.

00:05:13.148 --> 00:05:15.398
And it turns out you
can at a quantum level.

00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:16.788
We're talking on a scale of the stuff

00:05:16.788 --> 00:05:18.984
that make up atoms, strange things happen

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:19.850
at a quantum level.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:21.503
For one thing, all subatomic particles,

00:05:21.503 --> 00:05:23.686
they've got split personalities.

00:05:23.686 --> 00:05:26.378
One personality is a wave and
the other one's a particle,

00:05:26.378 --> 00:05:27.718
but there's still one being.

00:05:27.718 --> 00:05:28.978
When you wanna know where they are,

00:05:28.978 --> 00:05:30.048
they seem like a particle.

00:05:30.048 --> 00:05:31.588
And when you wanna know
what they're doing,

00:05:31.588 --> 00:05:32.978
they behave like waves,

00:05:32.978 --> 00:05:35.888
but you can't ask both
personalities at the same time.

00:05:35.888 --> 00:05:38.248
Basically they've got some
serious commitment issues

00:05:38.248 --> 00:05:39.701
and that means we can only
guess where they might be.

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:42.672
Imagine an electron has
to dice, six sides each

00:05:42.672 --> 00:05:44.088
what the electron rolls

00:05:44.088 --> 00:05:45.658
is where it will sit along the line.

00:05:45.658 --> 00:05:47.058
Our electron can't commit

00:05:47.058 --> 00:05:48.798
to a position until the dicer rolled.

00:05:48.798 --> 00:05:51.508
Remember there's commitment issues.

00:05:51.508 --> 00:05:53.458
So as our electronics shaking the dice,

00:05:53.458 --> 00:05:54.373
it's everywhere at once.

00:05:54.373 --> 00:05:57.358
Something like us trying
to measure its position,

00:05:57.358 --> 00:05:58.518
has to force the electron

00:05:58.518 --> 00:06:00.368
to let go of the dice and pick a spot.

00:06:00.368 --> 00:06:01.824
Of all combinations getting a seven

00:06:01.824 --> 00:06:03.767
is more likely than two or 12.

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.638
In reality, though, the electron

00:06:05.638 --> 00:06:07.248
can be in more than just 10 spots

00:06:07.248 --> 00:06:10.328
since there are many more
combinations than just two dice.

00:06:10.328 --> 00:06:12.238
Now we can pick your subatomic protocols

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:14.034
as this, a probability wave.

00:06:14.034 --> 00:06:16.108
This wave will tell us the odds

00:06:16.108 --> 00:06:18.058
of finding a particle at that location.

00:06:18.058 --> 00:06:20.198
Say, this is our electrons
probability wave.

00:06:20.198 --> 00:06:22.548
The peaks of the wave is
where we're most likely

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.278
to find the electron and in the valleys,

00:06:24.278 --> 00:06:26.008
it's less likely you'll find it there.

00:06:26.008 --> 00:06:28.298
Let's say the electron is
heading towards a barrier,

00:06:28.298 --> 00:06:30.558
as it hits the barrier,
the wave, it bounces off.

00:06:30.558 --> 00:06:32.086
But let me tell you something about waves.

00:06:32.086 --> 00:06:33.608
They are not perfect.

00:06:33.608 --> 00:06:35.338
For example, a beam of light

00:06:35.338 --> 00:06:37.205
doesn't perfectly reflect
off of the surface.

00:06:37.205 --> 00:06:39.222
A small fraction of light can get through.

00:06:39.222 --> 00:06:41.218
Waves won't bounce off perfectly

00:06:41.218 --> 00:06:42.531
so neither will the electron wave.

00:06:42.531 --> 00:06:45.295
Sometimes the wave can
slip through the barrier.

00:06:45.295 --> 00:06:47.038
When the wave is in the barrier,

00:06:47.038 --> 00:06:47.898
the chances of finding

00:06:47.898 --> 00:06:49.918
an electron there goes down by a lot.

00:06:49.918 --> 00:06:51.657
But if the barrier's thin enough,

00:06:51.657 --> 00:06:53.688
the wave you can reach the
other side before it dies off.

00:06:53.688 --> 00:06:55.087
So what does that mean?

00:06:55.087 --> 00:06:56.655
Remember the wave tells us how likely

00:06:56.655 --> 00:06:58.818
it is to find the electron there.

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:00.652
This means there's a chance
we can find our electron

00:07:00.652 --> 00:07:03.540
on the other side of the
barrier or in there too.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.572
Once it's on the other side,

00:07:04.572 --> 00:07:07.648
we can say the electron
tunneled through the barrier.

00:07:07.648 --> 00:07:08.768
This is quantum tunneling

00:07:08.768 --> 00:07:10.228
and that's how subatomic particles

00:07:10.228 --> 00:07:11.788
can walk through walls.

00:07:11.788 --> 00:07:14.808
Okay, so little elementary
particles can walk through walls,

00:07:14.808 --> 00:07:16.714
but I can't because my
body's made up of more

00:07:16.714 --> 00:07:19.148
than a quadrillion of
these quantum objects

00:07:19.148 --> 00:07:20.886
and the odds of all of them tunneling

00:07:20.886 --> 00:07:23.358
through the wall is
practically impossible.

00:07:23.358 --> 00:07:24.927
So why does quantum tumbling even matter?

00:07:24.927 --> 00:07:27.028
It's the reason we're alive.

00:07:27.028 --> 00:07:27.861
(giggling)

00:07:27.861 --> 00:07:30.138
Quantum tunneling allows nuclear fusion,

00:07:30.138 --> 00:07:30.971
sounds familiar?

00:07:30.971 --> 00:07:32.728
That's how our sun releases huge amounts

00:07:32.728 --> 00:07:35.331
of energy that makes life
on our planet possible.

00:07:35.331 --> 00:07:37.488
So how can you quantum tunnel at home?

00:07:37.488 --> 00:07:38.321
You already are.

00:07:38.321 --> 00:07:40.277
It's one of the ways our DNA mutates among

00:07:40.277 --> 00:07:43.488
other worlds that quantum
Physics plays in our Biology.

00:07:43.488 --> 00:07:44.918
Quantum Physics makes it seem like

00:07:44.918 --> 00:07:47.148
the world is playing cheat
codes on us, but it isn't.

00:07:47.148 --> 00:07:48.388
It's how the Universe works.

00:07:48.388 --> 00:07:50.878
Maybe the quantum world is telling us

00:07:50.878 --> 00:07:51.994
that when faced with an obstacle,

00:07:51.994 --> 00:07:54.472
there's a small chance
we can defy expectations

00:07:54.472 --> 00:07:56.333
and breach barriers.

00:07:56.333 --> 00:07:58.833
(piano music)

00:08:00.426 --> 00:08:02.759
(laughing)

